they pick up their ball . they hurry to their mom . they tell her about the fox . they hope they will see him again . they hope he will be their friend . lila was a princess who lived in a big palace . she had many toys and dresses and books , but she was not happy . she wanted to go outside and play with other children , but her father , the king , said no . he said it was too dangerous and she had to stay inside .

one day , lila saw a bird fly by her window . she opened the window and called to the bird . the bird came closer and landed on her hand . it was a blue bird with a yellow beak and a red tail . lila smiled and said hello to the bird . the bird said hello back and told her his name was riko .

lila and riko became friends . they talked and sang and played every day . riko told lila stories about the world outside the palace . he told her about the trees and the flowers and the animals and the people . lila wanted to see them with her own eyes . she asked riko to take her with him .

riko said yes , but he warned her that she had to be careful . he said she had to lie to her father and say she was sick . he said she had to wear a cloak and a hat to hide her face . he said she had to follow him and not talk to anyone . lila agreed . she was brave and curious .

the next morning , lila told her father that she felt bad . she said she had a headache and a sore throat . her father felt sorry for her and said she could stay in bed . he said he would send a doctor and a maid to take care of her . he kissed her forehead and left .

lila waited until the coast was clear . she put on a cloak and a hat and grabbed a basket . she opened the window and saw riko waiting for her . she climbed out and joined him . they flew away from the palace and into the sky .

lila felt free and happy . she saw many wonderful things with riko . she saw the green grass and the colorful flowers . she saw the fluffy clouds and the bright sun . she saw the friendly animals and the smiling people . she felt the warm breeze and the fresh air . she laughed and sang and played .

but she also saw some sad things . she saw the dirty streets and the broken houses . she saw the hungry children and the angry men . she saw the cold rain and the dark night . she felt the bitter cold and the fear .

lila realized that the world was not all good or all bad . it was both . she felt sorry for the people who had less than her . she felt grateful for the things she had . she felt love for riko and her father .

she decided to go back to the palace . she thanked riko for showing her the world . she hugged him and said goodbye . she promised to see him again . she climbed back into her window and into her bed .

she lied to her father and said she felt better . she smiled and said she had a good dream . she did not tell him about riko or the world . she kept it as a secret . she knew he would not understand . she knew he would be angry and scared .

she was happy and sad . she missed riko and the world . she loved her father and the palace . she was a princess who had seen both . she was a princess who had grown . lily and ben were jolly friends who liked to play outside . one day , they saw a big bird with white and black feathers . it was a swan . the swan was swimming in the lake near their house .

