one day , a small sock landed on the lion 's head and he did n't like it one bit . he roared and roared and chased the sock across the jungle .

the sock ducked and dodged around rocks and trees and the lion was so angry he roared even louder ! but the sock was too fast and he could n't catch it .

finally , the lion gave up and stopped roaring . he was tired and ready for a nap . but the sock was still there , sitting on his head .

the lion just laughed and shook his mane . he had forgotten all about chasing the sock and was happy to have a new , furry friend . the sock and the lion were friends ever after . the end . once , there was a little boy who wanted to take a nap . he laid down in the grass , closed his eyes , and was about to drift off . suddenly , he felt something cold wrapped around his wrist . he opened his eyes and saw a chain , coiled up and attached to his wrist . he felt so scared !

suddenly , an old man appeared beside him . he had a kind face and smiling eyes . he explained that the chain was made of stars and was put there to protect the boy while heâ€ ™ s napping . the boy calmed down and smiled . he thanked the old man , then began to take his nap again .

once he woke up , he went to show the chain to his mommy . she was both happy and bitter ; happy her son had found so much protection while asleep , yet bitter that he had been put in a place where something like this was necessary . but in the end , she thanked the stars that kept her son safe as he napped . once there was a little girl named mary . mary loved the ocean . she would play in the waves and collect shells .

