mom ran to them and hugged them . she was very angry and sad . she took them to the hospital . they had to stay there for many days . they could not watch their film . they were very sorry . they wished they had listened to mom . tim and lily were best friends . they liked to play in the park every day . they liked to slide , run , and climb . but they did not like to swing . they were fearful of the swing . they thought it was too high and too fast .

one day , a new boy came to the park . his name was sam . he saw tim and lily and said hello . he asked them if they wanted to swing with him . tim and lily shook their heads . they said they were scared of the swing .

sam smiled and said , " do n't be scared . the swing is fun . i will show you how to do it . you just sit on the seat , hold the ropes , and push with your feet . then you will rise in the air and feel the wind . it is like flying . come on , try it with me . "

tim and lily looked at each other . they wanted to be brave . they wanted to have fun . they decided to try the swing with sam . they followed him to the swing set . sam helped them sit on the seats and hold the ropes . he told them to push with their feet and lean back .

tim and lily did as sam said . they felt the swing move . they felt the air on their faces . they felt their hearts beat . they felt scared . but they also felt excited . they saw the trees and the sky . they heard sam laugh . they laughed too . they liked the swing . they were not fearful anymore . they thanked sam for showing them how to swing . they made a new friend . they had a good day . jill liked to help her mom in the garden . she liked to see the flowers and the fruits grow . she liked to smell the roses and taste the berries . she also liked to add water to the plants when they were thirsty .

one day , her mom gave her a small basket and a pair of scissors . she said , " jill , can you help me pick some prunes from the tree ? they are ripe and sweet . but be careful , the scissors are sharp . and do n't pick too many , we need to leave some for the birds and the squirrels . "

jill nodded and ran to the tree . she saw the prunes hanging from the branches . they were purple and round . she reached for one and cut it with the scissors . she put it in the basket . she did the same for another one , and another one . she was having fun .

she looked at the basket . it was almost full . she thought , maybe i can pick one more . she saw a big prune at the top of the tree . she wanted to get it . she climbed on a low branch and stretched her arm . she was about to cut it when she heard a voice .

" hey , that 's my prune ! " it was a squirrel . he was sitting on the branch next to the prune . he looked angry . he had a bushy tail and a small nose .

jill was surprised . she said , " i 'm sorry , i did n't know it was yours . i was helping my mom . she asked me to pick some prunes for us . "

the squirrel said , " well , you have enough prunes in your basket . you do n't need to take mine . i was saving it for later . it 's the biggest and the sweetest one in the tree . you are greedy . "

jill felt bad . she said , " i 'm not greedy . i 'm modest . i only wanted one more . but you are right . you can have it . i will leave it for you . i 'm sorry for bothering you . "

the squirrel said , " thank you . that 's very nice of you . i 'm sorry for being rude . you can have a small one if you want . there are plenty in the tree . we can share . "

jill smiled . she said , " thank you . that 's very kind of you . i will take a small one . and i will give you a berry from my basket . they are juicy and red . we can be friends . "

the squirrel smiled . he said , " thank you . that 's very generous of you . i will take a berry from your basket . they are delicious and bright . we can be friends . "

jill and the squirrel ate their prunes and berries . they talked and laughed . they enjoyed the sun and the breeze . they were happy . they were friends . lily was a little lamb who loved to eat hay . she always ate more hay than the other lambs , because she thought it was so yummy . she did not like to share her hay with anyone , not even her friends .

one day , she saw a big pile of hay in the barn . she ran to it and started to eat as much as she could . she did not notice that the pile was very high and unstable . she ate and ate , until she reached the top of the hay .

" wow , this is the best hay ever ! " she said to herself . " i am so lucky to have it all for me ! "

but then , the hay started to move . it was too heavy for the pile to hold . the hay fell down , and lily fell with it . she was buried under the hay , and she could not get out . she started to cry for help .

" help ! help ! i am stuck under the hay ! " she shouted .

the other lambs heard her cry . they ran to the barn and saw what had happened . they felt sorry for lily , but they also remembered how she never shared her hay with them .

" why should we help you ? " they asked . " you always ate all the hay by yourself . you did not care about us . you were greedy and selfish . "

lily realized that they were right . she had been greedy and selfish . she had not been a good friend . she felt very sorry and ashamed .

" please , please , help me ! " she begged . " i am sorry for what i did . i was wrong . i will share my hay with you from now on . i will be a good friend . please , forgive me ! "

the other lambs saw that lily was sincere . they decided to forgive her and help her . they worked together to move the hay and free lily . lily was very grateful and happy . she hugged the other lambs and thanked them .

" thank you , thank you , thank you ! " she said . " you are very kind and generous . you are my true friends . i will never be greedy and selfish again . i will share my hay with you , and we can eat it together . it will be more yummy that way ! "

the other lambs smiled and nodded . they were glad that lily had learned her lesson . they took some hay and ate it with lily . they enjoyed the hay and each other 's company . they were happy and content .

the moral of the story is : sharing is caring . greediness and selfishness can lead to trouble and loneliness . friendship and generosity can bring happiness and joy . mia was grumpy . she did not want to go to class . she wanted to stay at home and play with her toys . she pouted and crossed her arms .

