her mom was very sad and angry . she said jenny was being naughty and rude . she said jenny had to go to the party and she had no choice . she said jenny had to wear the green dress or she would get a time out . she said jenny had to stop crying and screaming and kicking .

but jenny refused . she did not listen to her mom . she did not care about the party . she did not care about the time out . she only cared about her yellow dress . she held on to her yellow dress and did not let go .

her mom gave up . she said jenny could wear her yellow dress , but she had to go to the party . she said jenny would miss all the fun and the cake and the games . she said jenny would make her friends sad and her mom ashamed . she said jenny would regret her choice .

but jenny refused . she did not believe her mom . she did not think the party would be fun . she did not want cake or games . she did not care about her friends or her mom . she only cared about her yellow dress . she put on her yellow dress and smiled .

she went to the party with her mom . she saw all the other kids wearing different colors . she saw the balloons and the streamers and the presents . she saw the clown and the magician and the pony . she saw the cake and the candles and the ice cream . she saw her friends laughing and playing and singing .

but jenny did not join them . she stayed by herself . she did not talk to anyone . she did not touch anything . she did not laugh or play or sing . she only held on to her yellow dress . she did not smile .

she realized her mom was right . the party was fun . the green dress was pretty . the yellow dress was boring . she wished she had listened to her mom . she wished she had worn the green dress . she wished she had been a good girl .

