they hugged the people and wished them well . they learned that it is good to help others who are poor and in trouble . they felt proud and happy . tom likes to play with his red ball . he can throw it high in the air and catch it . he can roll it on the ground and kick it . he can bounce it on the wall and clap his hands . he has a lot of fun with his red ball .

one day , tom goes to the park with his mom . he brings his red ball with him . he sees a big slide and wants to try it . he runs to the slide and puts his red ball on the ground . he climbs up the ladder and slides down . whee ! he feels happy and excited .

he slides again and again . he forgets about his red ball . he does not see a dog that comes to the park . the dog sees the red ball and thinks it is a toy . the dog runs to the ball and picks it up with his mouth . he runs away with the ball .

tom finishes sliding and looks for his red ball . he does not see it on the ground . he feels sad and confused . he asks his mom where his red ball is . his mom does not know . she tells him to look around the park .

tom looks everywhere . he looks behind the trees and under the benches . he looks in the swings and on the seesaw . he does not find his red ball . he feels angry and upset . he cries and says he wants his red ball back .

he hears a bark . he turns around and sees the dog . the dog has his red ball in his mouth . the dog is happy and playful . he wags his tail and drops the ball . he wants tom to play with him .

tom sees his red ball . he feels surprised and relieved . he runs to the ball and picks it up . he hugs it and says thank you to the dog . the dog barks and licks his face . he likes tom .

tom and the dog become friends . they play with the red ball together . they throw it high in the air and catch it . they roll it on the ground and kick it . they bounce it on the wall and clap their hands . they have a lot of fun with the red ball . anna and ben were going on a trip with their mom and dad . they were very happy and excited . they packed their bags with clothes , toys , and books . they said goodbye to their dog , spot , and got in the car .

the car drove for a long time . anna and ben looked out the window and saw many things . they saw trees , houses , farms , and bridges . they asked their mom and dad many questions . " where are we going ? " " how long will it take ? " " what will we see ? "

mom and dad smiled and said , " we are going to the harbor . it will take a few hours . we will see boats , water , and birds . we will stay in a hotel near the harbor . it will be fun ! "

anna and ben nodded and said , " wow ! that sounds great ! " they played with their toys and read their books . they sang songs and told jokes . they had a good time in the car .

finally , they arrived at the harbor . they saw many big and small boats . they saw blue water and white waves . they saw seagulls and pelicans . they heard horns and bells . they smelled fish and salt .

mom and dad parked the car and said , " we are here ! let 's go to the hotel and unpack our bags . then we can explore the harbor and have some ice cream . "

anna and ben cheered and said , " yay ! let 's go ! " they grabbed their bags and followed their mom and dad . they walked to the hotel and found their room . they unpacked their bags and put their things in the closet and drawers . they changed their clothes and put on their hats and sunglasses .

they were ready to go to the harbor . they ran to the door and said , " come on , mom and dad ! let 's go ! " they were not spoiled . they were just eager and curious . they loved the harbor and wanted to see more . they had a wonderful trip . lily and tom were friends who liked to play in the park . one day , they saw a big bell on a tower . lily wanted to ring the bell , but tom said no .

