the moral of this story is that everyone can be tall . when we do good things , like being kind and helping others , we will always be high . one day , two best friends were walking through the park . they saw a big tree and decided to lean against it . the taller one was curious and asked " why are we leaning on this tree ? " . the shorter one replied " because it feels good and it relaxes us " . while they were leaning , the shorter one began to feel a little pain in his back . he asked the taller one , " did you feel the same pain ? " . the taller one leaned in and said , " no , i did n't feel any pain " . he was curious to know why the smaller one felt pain , so the smaller one explained that they had been leaning on the tree too long and he was beginning to feel a bit stiff . the taller one thought that was a great idea , so they both moved away from the tree , and they felt much better . the moral of the story is to not stay in one position for too long or you may get a bit of pain . once upon a time , there were two good friends , jack and john . they went out to play one day , but then a problem arose . jack found a trunk with a lot of money in it . he wanted to keep it all for himself .

