they giggle and clap their hands . they have so much fun at the zoo . they love to see the animals , especially the ones that swim . lily liked to borrow books from the library . she liked to look at the pictures and learn new things . one day , she borrowed a book about animals . she wanted to know more about them .

at home , she showed the book to her brother tom . tom was older and could read . he said he would help her with the book . he said he would make a quiz for her . he asked her questions about the animals . lily tried to answer them .

some questions were easy , like what sound a dog makes . some questions were hard , like what animal has a powerful trunk . lily did not know what a trunk was . tom showed her a picture of an elephant . he said an elephant has a trunk . he said a trunk is like a long nose . lily thought that was funny .

lily liked the quiz . she learned a lot from the book and from tom . she said thank you to tom . she said she would borrow more books from the library . she said she wanted to know more about the world . tom said he was proud of her . he said he would help her again . they hugged and smiled . tom and mia were playing with their blocks in the living room . they liked to build towers and houses and cars with the blocks . sometimes they pretended to be giants and knocked down their buildings with their feet .

