anna and ben are happy . they hope the boy will change and be kind . they go back to the playground and have fun . they admire the birds and the flowers and the trees . they also like to run and jump and slide . they are good friends . ben likes to observe the birds in the park . he brings his binoculars and his book of bird names . he sits on a bench and waits for the birds to come . he sees a blue jay , a cardinal , a sparrow and a pigeon . he points to each one and says their name out loud .

one day , he sees a new bird . it is big and white and has a long neck . it makes a loud honk sound . ben does not know what it is . he looks in his book , but he can not find it . he is curious and excited . he wants to get closer to the new bird .

he gets off the bench and walks slowly towards the new bird . the new bird sees him and honks again . ben thinks it is saying hello . he says hello back . he reaches out his hand to touch the new bird . the new bird does not like that . it bites ben 's hand with its big beak . ben cries out in pain and runs back to the bench . he drops his binoculars and his book .

a lady who works in the park sees what happens . she runs to ben and helps him . she puts a band - aid on his hand and gives him a hug . she tells him that the new bird is a goose . she says that geese are not very friendly and do not like to be touched . she says that geese are popular in some places , but not in this park . she says that ben should observe them from far away and not bother them .

ben nods and says he is sorry . he says he will not touch the geese again . he says he will only observe the nice birds . he picks up his binoculars and his book . he thanks the lady and smiles . he still likes to observe the birds in the park , but he stays away from the geese . lily and ben are small kids who like to play together . they have many toys , but their favorite is a big red ball . they can kick it , throw it , roll it , and bounce it .

