one day , timmy wanted to explore the forest . he hopped and hopped until he came to a river . timmy wondered how to cross the river .

but then he saw a frog swimming in the river . timmy asked the frog a question .

" can you help me get across the river ? "

the frog smiled and said yes . he said he would show timmy the way . so timmy followed the frog , hopping from one rock to another until he was safely across the river .

when he was done , the frog said goodbye , and timmy hopped away . he was very happy that he could explore the forest without getting wet ! once upon a time there was a small girl . she was very obedient . one day she was playing in her yard when she saw a stranger . the girl was a bit scared but she was obedient and waited . the stranger walked up and said " hello " with a kind voice . the little girl still felt scared , so she turned and ran away .

the stranger then followed her . as she ran , his voice got kinder and gentler . he said " i just want to be your friend " . the little girl stopped running , and she started to feel better .

the stranger asked the girl if she would like to come with him and help pick some apples . the girl thought about it for a little bit , then she nodded her head and said " yes " . the two of them went to the closest orchard .

at the orchard , they picked as many apples as they could and they were both having fun . they picked apples until they were tired and the sun was setting . the little girl brought the apples home and helped her mom dry them .

once they were dry , they used the apples to make delicious apple pies and apple sauce . the little girl was happy and she thanked the stranger for his help . she said goodbye and watched the stranger walk away . the little girl never saw him again , but she always remembered him as a kind and obedient stranger . mummy and daddy had a lovely surprise for emma . they had bought her a plastic tape measure . emma was so excited ! she ran and squeezed the tape measure and saw the little red numbers go up and down . daddy taught emma how to measure things . she measured daddy 's hand and then the length of the table . mummy said with a giggle , " now you can measure all kinds of things ! " emma clapped her hands and said , " i love my tape measure ! " then emma went around the house measuring everything she could ! she even asked mummy and daddy if she could measure them , too ! daddy said , " you will be the best measurer in the world ! " emma smiled and said , " yes , i will be the best measurer ever ! " the radish was very shy . it did n't want to meet other vegetables in the garden . it stayed hidden in the shadows until it was all alone .

one day , a strong wind came and scattered the radish far away from the garden . it could n't believe what had happened . it was so frightened .

the radish rolled all the way down the hill and landed in a different garden . everyone was so friendly and welcoming . the radish felt shy at first , but soon became part of the group . it felt like it belonged .

the radishes in the new garden were so different . they played , laughed and had so much fun in the sun . the shy radish soon realised that it had been missing out all this time ! little sue was so excited . she was going to visit the hill today . as she packed her picnic basket , the sun came out in the sky . she put on her sun hat and skipped outside ready to explore the hill .

as she started to climb the hill , it got steeper and steeper . she stopped and looked up . it looked like it was a long way to the top . sue hesitated for a moment , but then decided she was ready for the challenge .

